{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>There is little Benjamin their ruler</b> — in number, for the time was near to the matter of the concubine in Gibeah, or on account of his being the youngest of all the sons." "<b>And the meaning of רודם</b> — the one who rules them (הרודה שיש להם), and the mem is a sign of plural groups, and it comes with kamatz qaton under [a] gadol, like המעלם מים." "<b>ורגמתם</b> — like שרים, and likewise רגם מלך, and I have already mentioned this verse at the beginning of the psalm."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 68, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra cites the form המעלם (Judges 5:30) where the mem functions as a plural suffix on a singular form; 'kamatz qaton under gadol' refers to a short kamatz where a long kamatz (gadol) would normally appear in the singular form."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:16.762086527Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}